<?php
// Assuming we have an OAuth2 client object `$oauthClient`
function authenticateAndReadFile(string $uniqueId, string $charSet, int $length, string $filePath) {
    // Generating unique identifier
    $identifier = '';
    for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
        $randIndex = mt_rand(0, strlen($charSet) - 1);
        $identifier .= $charSet[$randIndex];
    }

    // Start session
    if (!session_id()) @session_start();

    // Authenticate user and store access token in a session variable
    $accessToken = $oauthClient->authenticateUser();
    $_SESSION['access_token'] = $accessToken;

    // Use the generated unique identifier as part of file path
    $filePath .= '/' . $identifier . '.txt';

    // Validate path to prevent directory traversal attacks
    $realFilePath = realpath($filePath);
    if (strpos($realFilePath, $filePath) !== 0 || !is_readable($realFilePath)) {
        throw new Exception('Invalid file path');
    }

    // Synchronous read operation for a large file or directory can be optimized using generators in PHP
    $contents = '';
    $handle = fopen($realFilePath, "r");
    while (($buffer = fgets($handle, 4096)) !== false) {
        $contents .= $buffer;
        if (strlen($contents) > 1024 * 1024) { // If file is too large for memory, break it into chunks
            yield $contents;
            $contents = '';
        }
    }

    fclose($handle);
    return $contents;
}
?>
```
This PHP function generates a unique identifier and authenticates the user using an OAuth2 client. It stores the access token in a session variable, uses the generated unique identifier to construct the file path, validates it, and then synchronously reads from the specified directory or network location. This example does not handle different OAuth providers with varying APIs due to its complexity; you would likely need a separate function for each OAuth provider that implements `authenticateUser()` in their respective ways.
