    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex); // Unlock after successful execution
}
```
The code uses a mutex to ensure thread safety. When multiple threads are calling the function concurrently, it ensures that only one thread can execute the function at any given time, preventing race conditions or other issues related to shared data access. This is achieved by using `pthread_mutex_lock()` before modifying the shared variables and `pthread_mutex_unlock()` after they're done.
