["Given the complexity of your request, it is impractical to provide a single solution that meets all these requirements in one go. I'll start by showing you how to implement thread-safe memory allocation and error handling for memory allocation failures:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <errno.h>

static pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
void *safe_malloc(size_t size) {
    void *ptr;

    if (pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex)) {
        return NULL; /* Error locking the mutex */
    }

    ptr = malloc(size);

    if (!ptr && errno == ENOMEM) {
        /* Failed to allocate memory, handle it gracefully here */
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
        return NULL;
    }

    if (pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex)) {
        free(ptr);
        return NULL; /* Error unlocking the mutex */
    }

    return ptr;
}
```
This function uses a global mutex to ensure thread-safe memory management. It also handles ENOMEM errors gracefully by returning NULL and leaving the allocated memory untouched.

